    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0163" n="151" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12297: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-22T06:00:00+02:00">June 22, 1941—6
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 22—5:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2484. At 5:30 this morning, German summer time, Goebbels,<anchor n="87"
                        xml:id="d155-f1"/> read on the radio a proclamation of the Reich Chancellor
                    to the German people outlining the course of German-Russian relations since the
                    beginning of the war and announcing the inauguration of military action against
                    Russia on the entire front from the Arctic Ocean to the Black Sea.<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d155-f2"/> It was stated that the armed force of Finland and Rumania
                    would participate in the German effort.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="87" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
                <p>Josef Goebbels, Reich Minister of Propaganda.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d155-f2" n="88" xml:id="d155-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the German statement, see the <hi rendition="#italic">New York
                        Times</hi>, June 22, 1941, p. 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
